# PoetryDB search, live: a suggested poet, results grouped by poet and paged,
# a poem opened and turned, kept as a favourite, More by this poet, and a card
# made from a searched poem. Assertions stay on what PoetryDB has held for
# years: Keats's poems and their line counts.
wait-for-id poem-menu
wait-idle 3000
tap Browse
wait-for Poems
tap Search
wait-for Poets to start with
tap John Keats
wait-for poems for
wait-idle
expect John Keats
expect A Thing of Beauty
expect lines ·
expect 1 of
clean
shot results
tap-id list-next
wait-for 2 of
clean
shot results-page-two
tap-paged In Drear-Nighted December
wait-for In drear-nighted December
wait-idle
expect John Keats
clean
shot searched-poem
tap-id online-next
wait-idle
expect From PoetryDB
clean
shot searched-poem-last-page
# A searched poem kept as a favourite is on the shelf, and opens from it.
tap-id poem-menu
wait-for Make a quote card
tap Favorite
wait-idle
expect Remove favorite
# The card of a searched poem says where its words came from.
wait-for Make a quote card
tap Make a quote card
wait-for Saved for your computer
expect In Drear-Nighted December, John Keats
clean
shot searched-card
tap Back
wait-idle
tap More by this poet
wait-for poems for
wait-idle
expect A Thing of Beauty
tap Back
wait-for Favorites
expect In Drear-Nighted December
clean
shot browse-searched-favourite
# Offline, the kept poem still opens, and a search says the reader is
# offline rather than that nothing matched.
scenario offline
tap In Drear-Nighted December
wait-for In drear-nighted December
tap Back
wait-for Favorites
tap Search
wait-for Poets to start with
tap William Blake
wait-for This reader is offline
expect-missing No poems found
clean
shot search-offline
scenario normal
# A typed search that matches nothing says only that, with no error over it.
tap Search
wait-for Poets to start with
tap-id scope-line
expect Words from a line
tap-id search-field
wait-for Type here
type qzxv
tap Search
wait-for No poems found
clean
shot no-matches
expect-missing couldn't open
